395
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:12,130
perfect. So, Jack, how are you feeling today? I'm feeling great. I'm excited because this

396
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:18,610
topic can really change how people communicate at work. I agree. Okay, everyone, let's get

397
00:18:18,610 --> 00:18:25,410
started. Let's begin with something simple. What is negotiation? Good question. Negotiation

398
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:31,130
is when two or more people discuss something to reach an agreement. Exactly. It could

399
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:36,150
be about price, deadlines, responsibilities, or even ideas.

400
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:41,190
And in business, negotiation needs to be polite, clear, and professional.

401
00:18:41,190 --> 00:18:44,550
So let's start with how to open a negotiation.

402
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:45,550
Yes.

403
00:18:45,550 --> 00:18:48,070
First impressions are very important.

404
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:50,790
You want to sound friendly, but professional.

405
00:18:50,790 --> 00:18:54,790
A simple phrase could be, thank you for meeting with us today.

406
00:18:54,790 --> 00:18:58,870
Or we appreciate the opportunity to discuss this project.

407
00:18:58,870 --> 00:19:02,590
Another useful phrase is, let's go over the main points.

408
00:19:02,590 --> 00:19:05,790
Yes, that helps guide the conversation.

409
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:07,190
Let's do a quick example.

410
00:19:07,190 --> 00:19:08,190
I'll start.

411
00:19:08,190 --> 00:19:09,190
Okay.

412
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:11,150
Thank you for meeting with us today.

413
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,870
We're excited to discuss this partnership.

414
00:19:13,870 --> 00:19:14,870
Thank you.

415
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:16,550
We appreciate your interest.

416
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:18,310
Let's go over your proposal.

417
00:19:18,310 --> 00:19:20,470
That sounds natural and professional.

418
00:19:20,470 --> 00:19:22,590
Yes, and very simple.

419
00:19:22,590 --> 00:19:25,690
Now let's talk about making your first offer.

420
00:19:25,690 --> 00:19:28,150
This is where many people feel nervous.

421
00:19:28,150 --> 00:19:31,550
True, but you don't need complicated language.

422
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:35,990
For example, you can say, we would like to wait.

423
00:19:35,990 --> 00:19:37,310
Let's correct that.

424
00:19:37,310 --> 00:19:39,470
We would like to propose.

425
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:40,470
Good correction.

426
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:44,390
Or, you can say, our initial offer is...

427
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:48,470
Another useful phrase is, we're looking at a budget of...

428
00:19:48,470 --> 00:19:49,830
Let's give an example.

429
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:50,830
Sure.

430
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:54,710
Our initial offer is $50,000 for the project.

431
00:19:54,710 --> 00:19:56,150
Thank you for your offer.

432
00:19:56,150 --> 00:19:57,710
Let me review that.

433
00:19:57,710 --> 00:20:00,110
That's how calm and polite that sounds.

434
00:20:00,110 --> 00:20:03,910
Yes, no pressure, just clear communication.

435
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:06,030
Now let's talk about agreeing.

436
00:20:06,030 --> 00:20:07,790
This is the easy part, right?

437
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:11,030
Yes, but we still want to sound professional.

438
00:20:11,030 --> 00:20:15,590
Instead of just saying, okay, you can say, that sounds reasonable.

439
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:18,030
Or we're happy with that arrangement.

440
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:21,230
Another good one is, I think that works for us.

441
00:20:21,230 --> 00:20:22,430
Let's practice.

442
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:25,350
We can deliver the project in four weeks.

443
00:20:25,350 --> 00:20:26,790
That sounds reasonable.

444
00:20:26,790 --> 00:20:33,270
happy with that timeline. Perfect. Now what about disagreeing? This is more difficult.

445
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:40,510
Yes, because you don't want to sound rude. Exactly. So instead of saying no, that's wrong,

446
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:46,950
you soften your language. For example, I'm afraid that won't work for us. Or we see it

447
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:52,590
a bit differently. Another great phrase is I understand your point, but let's try

448
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:58,950
example. We'd like to reduce the budget by 20%. I understand your point but that

449
00:20:58,950 --> 00:21:04,430
would be difficult for us. That's polite and professional. Yes and it keeps the

450
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:10,070
conversation positive. Now let's talk about making counter offers. This is very

451
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:15,070
important in negotiation. A counter offer is when you respond with a different

452
00:21:15,070 --> 00:21:21,950
suggestion. You can say would you be open to or we could consider another

453
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:25,230
Another good one is, what if we...

454
00:21:25,230 --> 00:21:26,230
Example time.

455
00:21:26,230 --> 00:21:28,910
We can only pay $40,000.

456
00:21:28,910 --> 00:21:30,110
I see.

457
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:35,430
Would you be open to $45,000 if we include additional services?

458
00:21:35,430 --> 00:21:37,790
That's a strong negotiation move.

459
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:38,790
Yes.

460
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:41,790
You're not saying no, you're offering a solution.

461
00:21:41,790 --> 00:21:45,230
Now let's talk about asking for clarification.

462
00:21:45,230 --> 00:21:46,390
Very important.

463
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:48,870
You should never guess in business.

464
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:49,870
Exactly.

465
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:55,850
You can say, could you clarify that or can you explain what you mean by that?

466
00:21:55,850 --> 00:21:59,030
Another one is just to make sure I understand.

467
00:21:59,030 --> 00:22:00,190
Let's practice.

468
00:22:00,190 --> 00:22:03,390
We expect delivery in a short frame time.

469
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:07,630
Just to make sure I understand, what timeline are you expecting?

470
00:22:07,630 --> 00:22:08,630
Perfect.

471
00:22:08,630 --> 00:22:12,030
Now let's talk about delaying or thinking time.

472
00:22:12,030 --> 00:22:15,190
Yes, sometimes you need time to decide.

473
00:22:15,190 --> 00:22:21,730
You can say, let me think about that, or we need some time to review this internally.

474
00:22:21,730 --> 00:22:24,710
Another one is, can we get back to you on that?

475
00:22:24,710 --> 00:22:27,990
Example, can you confirm the deal today?

476
00:22:27,990 --> 00:22:30,950
We need some time to review this internally.

477
00:22:30,950 --> 00:22:32,950
We'll get back to you tomorrow.

478
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:34,710
That's very professional.

479
00:22:34,710 --> 00:22:37,590
Now let's move into a longer role play.

480
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,590
Great idea.

481
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:40,950
This will help everyone see everything together.

482
00:22:40,950 --> 00:22:43,830
Hi, thank you for meeting with us today.

483
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:44,830
Thank you.

484
00:22:44,830 --> 00:22:46,830
We decided to discuss this opportunity.

485
00:22:46,830 --> 00:22:48,830
Let's start with your proposal.

486
00:22:48,830 --> 00:22:55,830
Sure. Our initial offer is $60,000 including full support and delivery in six weeks.

487
00:22:55,830 --> 00:22:58,830
I see. That's a bit higher than our budget.

488
00:22:58,830 --> 00:23:02,830
I understand your concern. What budget are you working with?

489
00:23:02,830 --> 00:23:05,830
We were hoping for something closer to $50,000.

490
00:23:05,830 --> 00:23:11,830
I see. Would you be open to $55,000 if we adjust the scope slightly?

491
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:15,830
That sounds reasonable. What changes would you suggest?

492
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:19,830
We could reduce the number of revisions and extend the timeline slightly.

493
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:22,830
Okay. That could work. Let me think about it.

494
00:23:22,830 --> 00:23:24,830
Of course. Take your time.

495
00:23:24,830 --> 00:23:29,830
Actually, I think we can agree to $55,000 with those conditions.

496
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:31,830
Great. We're happy to move forward.

497
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:33,830
That was a great negotiation.

498
00:23:33,830 --> 00:23:37,830
Yes. And notice how polite and clear everything was.

499
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:42,290
That's the key to successful negotiation in English.

500
00:23:42,290 --> 00:23:44,010
Keep your language simple.

501
00:23:44,010 --> 00:23:46,010
Stay calm and respectful.

502
00:23:46,010 --> 00:23:48,690
And always focus on solutions.

