535
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:24,010
Yes, they might have good ideas, but they don't know how to express them clearly

536
00:25:24,010 --> 00:25:25,250
or politely.

537
00:25:25,250 --> 00:25:28,970
Or they worry about sounding too direct or too weak.

538
00:25:28,970 --> 00:25:29,970
Exactly.

539
00:25:29,970 --> 00:25:35,250
Today we'll teach you practical phrases you can use immediately in real business meetings.

540
00:25:35,250 --> 00:25:40,610
And we'll also do role plays so you can see how these phrases work in real conversations.

541
00:25:40,610 --> 00:25:41,610
Perfect.

542
00:25:41,610 --> 00:25:42,610
So let's get started.

543
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:46,050
All right, Jamie, let's begin with a simple question.

544
00:25:46,050 --> 00:25:48,570
What is negotiation in business?

545
00:25:48,570 --> 00:25:50,290
Great question.

546
00:25:50,290 --> 00:25:54,170
Negotiation is when two or more people discuss something to reach an agreement.

547
00:25:54,170 --> 00:25:56,490
So it's not about winning, right?

548
00:25:56,490 --> 00:25:57,490
Exactly.

549
00:25:57,490 --> 00:26:00,070
finding a solution that works for everyone.

550
00:26:00,070 --> 00:26:01,930
That's a very important mindset.

551
00:26:01,930 --> 00:26:06,290
Yes, good negotiation is about collaboration, not conflict.

552
00:26:06,290 --> 00:26:10,570
Okay, so let's start with the beginning of a negotiation.

553
00:26:10,570 --> 00:26:11,830
Imagine you're in a meeting.

554
00:26:11,830 --> 00:26:13,830
How do you introduce your position?

555
00:26:13,830 --> 00:26:17,570
You can use simple and polite phrases like from our perspective.

556
00:26:17,570 --> 00:26:19,370
Ah, that sounds professional.

557
00:26:19,370 --> 00:26:24,410
Yes, for example, from our perspective, this timeline is a bit too short.

558
00:26:24,410 --> 00:26:26,970
That's very clear, but not aggressive.

559
00:26:26,970 --> 00:26:30,170
Exactly. Another phrase is, we believe that.

560
00:26:30,170 --> 00:26:34,170
For example, we believe that this approach will be more effective.

561
00:26:34,170 --> 00:26:37,770
Perfect. You can also say, our main concern is...

562
00:26:37,770 --> 00:26:40,270
That sounds useful. Can you give an example?

563
00:26:40,270 --> 00:26:43,970
Sure. Our main concern is the cost of implementation.

564
00:26:43,970 --> 00:26:46,970
That's great. You're expressing a problem clearly.

565
00:26:46,970 --> 00:26:49,170
Yes, and you're doing it politely.

566
00:26:49,170 --> 00:26:52,870
Now, what if you want to ask the other person for their opinion?

567
00:26:52,870 --> 00:26:56,270
Good point. Negotiation is a two-way conversation.

568
00:26:56,270 --> 00:26:58,730
You can say, what are your thoughts on this?

569
00:26:58,730 --> 00:26:59,890
Simple and natural.

570
00:26:59,890 --> 00:27:01,890
Or how do you see this situation?

571
00:27:01,890 --> 00:27:02,890
I like that.

572
00:27:02,890 --> 00:27:04,430
It sounds very professional.

573
00:27:04,430 --> 00:27:08,150
You can also say, would you be open to discussing this further?

574
00:27:08,150 --> 00:27:09,150
That's very polite.

575
00:27:09,150 --> 00:27:10,150
Yes.

576
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:12,710
It invites discussion instead of forcing agreement.

577
00:27:12,710 --> 00:27:15,150
Now, let's talk about agreeing.

578
00:27:15,150 --> 00:27:17,490
What phrases can we use when we agree?

579
00:27:17,490 --> 00:27:19,510
You can say, that sounds reasonable.

580
00:27:19,510 --> 00:27:20,710
That's a great one.

581
00:27:20,710 --> 00:27:22,770
Or I completely agree with you.

582
00:27:22,770 --> 00:27:24,110
Very clear.

583
00:27:24,110 --> 00:27:26,750
Another useful one is that makes sense.

584
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:28,050
Simple and defective.

585
00:27:28,050 --> 00:27:30,910
You can also say we're on the same page.

586
00:27:30,910 --> 00:27:32,990
That's a very common business expression.

587
00:27:32,990 --> 00:27:36,030
Yes, it means you both understand and agree.

588
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:38,230
Now what about partial agreement?

589
00:27:38,230 --> 00:27:40,230
Ah, that's very important.

590
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:42,030
You don't always fully agree.

591
00:27:42,030 --> 00:27:43,190
Exactly.

592
00:27:43,190 --> 00:27:45,950
You can say I see your point, but...

593
00:27:45,950 --> 00:27:47,550
That's a classic phrase.

594
00:27:47,550 --> 00:27:52,230
For example, I see your point, but we need more time to complete the project.

595
00:27:52,230 --> 00:27:53,810
That's very balanced.

596
00:27:53,810 --> 00:27:56,470
Another one is, I agree to some extent.

597
00:27:56,470 --> 00:27:57,470
Nice.

598
00:27:57,470 --> 00:28:00,110
Or that's a good point, however.

599
00:28:00,110 --> 00:28:01,550
Very professional language.

600
00:28:01,550 --> 00:28:04,550
Yes, it helps you disagree politely.

601
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:08,310
Speaking of that, how do we disagree in a professional way?

602
00:28:08,310 --> 00:28:09,870
This is very important.

603
00:28:09,870 --> 00:28:11,670
You should never sound rude.

604
00:28:11,670 --> 00:28:12,750
Absolutely.

605
00:28:12,750 --> 00:28:15,590
You can say, I'm not sure I agree with that.

606
00:28:15,590 --> 00:28:17,350
That's soft and polite.

607
00:28:17,350 --> 00:28:19,150
Or I see it differently.

608
00:28:19,150 --> 00:28:20,510
That's very nice.

609
00:28:20,510 --> 00:28:24,290
Another one is, I understand your point, but I have a different view.

610
00:28:24,290 --> 00:28:25,790
That's perfect for meetings.

611
00:28:25,790 --> 00:28:28,990
Yes, it shows respect while expressing disagreement.

612
00:28:28,990 --> 00:28:31,850
Now, let's talk about making suggestions.

613
00:28:31,850 --> 00:28:32,850
Great.

614
00:28:32,850 --> 00:28:34,250
You can say, what if we…

615
00:28:34,250 --> 00:28:38,150
For example, what if we extend the deadline by one week?

616
00:28:38,150 --> 00:28:39,150
Exactly.

617
00:28:39,150 --> 00:28:40,510
Or how about we…

618
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:43,070
How about we reduce the budget slightly?

619
00:28:43,070 --> 00:28:44,150
Perfect.

620
00:28:44,150 --> 00:28:46,830
Another useful phrase is, we could consider…

621
00:28:46,830 --> 00:28:48,390
That sounds very professional.

622
00:28:48,390 --> 00:28:51,990
Yes, for example, we could consider a phased approach.

623
00:28:51,990 --> 00:28:53,150
That's excellent.

624
00:28:53,150 --> 00:28:55,790
You can also say one option might be

625
00:28:55,790 --> 00:28:57,590
Very flexible language.

626
00:28:57,590 --> 00:29:00,110
Yes, it shows you are open to discussion.

627
00:29:00,110 --> 00:29:03,950
Now, what if you want to negotiate or make a compromise?

628
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:06,190
This is the heart of negotiation.

629
00:29:06,190 --> 00:29:08,550
You can say, would you be willing to

630
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:11,750
For example, would you be willing to lower the price?

631
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:14,750
Exactly, or if we do this, could you

632
00:29:14,750 --> 00:29:17,630
Ah, that's conditional negotiation.

633
00:29:17,630 --> 00:29:21,870
Yes. For example, if we increase the order, could you offer a discount?

634
00:29:21,870 --> 00:29:23,470
That's very realistic.

635
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:26,910
Another one is we're prepared to, provided that.

636
00:29:26,910 --> 00:29:28,590
That sounds advanced.

637
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:31,870
Yes. For example, we're prepared to sign the contract,

638
00:29:31,870 --> 00:29:34,670
provided that the delivery time is reduced.

639
00:29:34,670 --> 00:29:36,590
That's a powerful phrase.

640
00:29:36,590 --> 00:29:38,990
Yes. It clearly shows your condition.

641
00:29:38,990 --> 00:29:41,710
Now, let's talk about handling problems.

642
00:29:41,710 --> 00:29:45,390
Good idea. You can say we're facing some challenges with.

643
00:29:45,390 --> 00:29:49,070
For example, we're facing some challenges with the timeline.

644
00:29:49,070 --> 00:29:52,270
Exactly. Or there seems to be an issue with…

645
00:29:52,270 --> 00:29:53,470
Very polite.

646
00:29:53,470 --> 00:29:55,950
Another one is we need to address…

647
00:29:55,950 --> 00:29:58,270
That sounds serious, but professional.

648
00:29:58,270 --> 00:30:00,110
Yes, it shows action.

649
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:02,350
Now, let's move to a role play.

650
00:30:02,350 --> 00:30:05,870
Great idea. Let's imagine a business meeting negotiation.

651
00:30:05,870 --> 00:30:09,070
I'll be a client and you'll be a project manager.

652
00:30:09,070 --> 00:30:10,270
Perfect. Let's start.

653
00:30:10,270 --> 00:30:11,950
Thank you for meeting with us today.

654
00:30:11,950 --> 00:30:15,230
Thank you for having me. We're excited to discuss the project.

655
00:30:15,230 --> 00:30:18,350
From our perspective, the timeline is quite tight.

656
00:30:18,350 --> 00:30:20,110
I understand your concern.

657
00:30:20,110 --> 00:30:23,870
However, we believe the timeline is achievable with proper planning.

658
00:30:23,870 --> 00:30:27,070
I see your point, but we're worried about quality.

659
00:30:27,070 --> 00:30:28,670
That's a valid concern.

660
00:30:28,670 --> 00:30:31,070
What if we add an extra review phase?

661
00:30:31,070 --> 00:30:32,590
That sounds reasonable.

662
00:30:32,590 --> 00:30:34,270
How would that affect the cost?

663
00:30:34,270 --> 00:30:36,510
It would increase the cost slightly.

664
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:39,390
However, we could adjust other areas to balance it.

665
00:30:39,390 --> 00:30:40,830
Could you give an example?

666
00:30:40,830 --> 00:30:43,630
Sure, we could reduce the number of revisions.

667
00:30:43,630 --> 00:30:45,630
I'm not sure I agree with that.

668
00:30:45,630 --> 00:30:47,630
Revisions are important for us.

669
00:30:47,630 --> 00:30:52,630
I understand. In that case, we could consider extending the timeline instead.

670
00:30:52,630 --> 00:30:55,630
That might work. How much extra time would you need?

671
00:30:55,630 --> 00:30:57,630
Approximately one additional week.

672
00:30:57,630 --> 00:30:59,630
That sounds acceptable.

673
00:30:59,630 --> 00:31:01,630
Great. So we're on the same page?

674
00:31:01,630 --> 00:31:02,630
Yes, I believe so.

675
00:31:02,630 --> 00:31:03,630
Excellent.

676
00:31:03,630 --> 00:31:05,630
That was a great example.

677
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:07,630
Yes, very realistic.

678
00:31:07,630 --> 00:31:10,630
Let's do another one. Maybe a price negotiation.

679
00:31:10,630 --> 00:31:11,630
Perfect.

680
00:31:11,630 --> 00:31:15,470
The proposal looks good, but the price is a bit high for us.

681
00:31:15,470 --> 00:31:17,310
I understand your concern.

682
00:31:17,310 --> 00:31:18,990
Could you share your budget range?

683
00:31:18,990 --> 00:31:22,470
We were hoping for something closer to $8,000.

684
00:31:22,470 --> 00:31:23,470
I see.

685
00:31:23,470 --> 00:31:25,390
Our current price is $10,000.

686
00:31:25,390 --> 00:31:30,150
However, we could offer a discount if you commit to a long-term contract.

687
00:31:30,150 --> 00:31:31,230
That's interesting.

688
00:31:31,230 --> 00:31:33,390
What kind of discount are we talking about?

689
00:31:33,390 --> 00:31:35,230
We could reduce the price by 10%.

690
00:31:35,230 --> 00:31:38,870
That's a good start, but it's still above our budget.

691
00:31:38,870 --> 00:31:42,130
In that case, we could adjust the scope of the project.

692
00:31:42,130 --> 00:31:43,390
What do you suggest?

693
00:31:43,390 --> 00:31:46,050
We could remove some non-essential features.

694
00:31:46,050 --> 00:31:47,190
That might work.

695
00:31:47,190 --> 00:31:48,510
Would you be open to that?

696
00:31:48,510 --> 00:31:51,030
Yes, I think that's a reasonable solution.

697
00:31:51,030 --> 00:31:52,030
Great.

698
00:31:52,030 --> 00:31:53,190
That was very practical.

699
00:31:53,190 --> 00:31:56,530
Yes, these are real situations people face.

700
00:31:56,530 --> 00:31:59,470
Before we finish, let's give some final tips.

701
00:31:59,470 --> 00:32:00,470
Sure.

702
00:32:00,470 --> 00:32:02,230
First, always stay polite.

703
00:32:02,230 --> 00:32:05,950
Second, be clear and direct, but not aggressive.

704
00:32:05,950 --> 00:32:08,830
Third, listen carefully to the other person.

705
00:32:08,830 --> 00:32:11,830
be flexible and open to compromise.

706
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:14,830
And finally, practice these phrases regularly.

707
00:32:14,830 --> 00:32:16,830
Practice really makes a difference.

708
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:17,830
Absolutely.

