00:42:52,710 --> 00:42:55,430
So Alex, what are we talking about today?

923
00:42:55,430 --> 00:43:00,830
Today we're diving into a very powerful and practical topic, negotiation phrases for business

924
00:43:00,830 --> 00:43:01,830
meetings.

925
00:43:01,830 --> 00:43:04,410
Oh, I love this topic.

926
00:43:04,410 --> 00:43:09,910
Negotiation is something we all face, whether it's discussing prices, deadlines, responsibilities,

927
00:43:09,910 --> 00:43:11,430
or project terms.

928
00:43:11,430 --> 00:43:12,510
Exactly.

929
00:43:12,510 --> 00:43:16,550
And the key is not just what you say, but how you say it.

930
00:43:16,550 --> 00:43:17,550
That's right.

931
00:43:17,550 --> 00:43:21,850
to sound polite, confident, and professional at the same time.

932
00:43:21,850 --> 00:43:26,850
And don't worry, we're going to make it simple and practical with lots of real examples.

933
00:43:26,850 --> 00:43:27,850
Sounds perfect.

934
00:43:27,850 --> 00:43:30,050
So Alex, how are you feeling today?

935
00:43:30,050 --> 00:43:31,250
I'm feeling great.

936
00:43:31,250 --> 00:43:33,130
Ready to negotiate some ideas.

937
00:43:33,130 --> 00:43:34,130
How about you?

938
00:43:34,130 --> 00:43:35,250
I'm doing really well.

939
00:43:35,250 --> 00:43:39,770
I'm excited because this is something learners can use immediately at work.

940
00:43:39,770 --> 00:43:40,770
Totally agree.

941
00:43:40,770 --> 00:43:43,370
All right, everyone, let's get started.

942
00:43:43,370 --> 00:43:45,650
Let's begin with a simple question.

943
00:43:45,650 --> 00:43:48,690
What is negotiation in a business meeting?

944
00:43:48,690 --> 00:43:50,390
Good question.

945
00:43:50,390 --> 00:43:54,330
Negotiation is when two or more people discuss something to reach an agreement.

946
00:43:54,330 --> 00:43:57,570
So it's not about winning or losing, right?

947
00:43:57,570 --> 00:43:58,570
Exactly.

948
00:43:58,570 --> 00:44:01,770
It's about finding a solution that works for everyone.

949
00:44:01,770 --> 00:44:03,530
That's very important.

950
00:44:03,530 --> 00:44:07,130
Many people think negotiation is about being aggressive.

951
00:44:07,130 --> 00:44:11,510
But actually, it's about communication, understanding, and compromise.

952
00:44:11,510 --> 00:44:15,230
So let's start with the beginning of a negotiation.

953
00:44:15,230 --> 00:44:20,070
you're in a meeting, how do you start? A good way to start is by setting a positive

954
00:44:20,070 --> 00:44:25,430
tone. For example, you can say, thank you for meeting with us today. Yes, that sounds

955
00:44:25,430 --> 00:44:30,790
polite and professional. You can also say, we appreciate the opportunity to discuss this

956
00:44:30,790 --> 00:44:36,310
with you. That's a great phrase. It shows respect. Another one is, let's see how

957
00:44:36,310 --> 00:44:41,750
we can find a solution that works for both sides. I like that. It shows cooperation

958
00:44:41,750 --> 00:44:43,230
from the beginning.

959
00:44:43,230 --> 00:44:45,870
Now let's say you want to introduce your position.

960
00:44:45,870 --> 00:44:46,870
Right.

961
00:44:46,870 --> 00:44:49,390
You want to explain what you want clearly.

962
00:44:49,390 --> 00:44:52,790
You can say, from our perspective, we believe that...

963
00:44:52,790 --> 00:44:55,270
Or our main objective is to...

964
00:44:55,270 --> 00:44:56,670
Exactly.

965
00:44:56,670 --> 00:45:00,550
Another useful phrase is, what we're aiming for is...

966
00:45:00,550 --> 00:45:03,950
These phrases sound very natural in business meetings.

967
00:45:03,950 --> 00:45:06,470
Now let's talk about making suggestions.

968
00:45:06,470 --> 00:45:07,470
Yes.

969
00:45:07,470 --> 00:45:10,190
This is very important in negotiations.

970
00:45:10,190 --> 00:45:13,030
You can say, how about we consider...

971
00:45:13,030 --> 00:45:15,710
Or would you be open to...

972
00:45:15,710 --> 00:45:18,590
That's a very polite way to suggest something.

973
00:45:18,590 --> 00:45:21,150
Another one is, what if we try...

974
00:45:21,150 --> 00:45:22,150
Perfect.

975
00:45:22,150 --> 00:45:26,190
These phrases invite discussion instead of forcing an idea.

976
00:45:26,190 --> 00:45:28,030
Let's do a quick example.

977
00:45:28,030 --> 00:45:29,030
Great idea.

978
00:45:29,030 --> 00:45:30,030
I'll start.

979
00:45:30,030 --> 00:45:33,430
We'd like the project to be completed in two weeks.

980
00:45:33,430 --> 00:45:37,550
I understand your timeline, but would you be open to extending it to three weeks

981
00:45:37,550 --> 00:45:39,350
to ensure quality?

982
00:45:39,350 --> 00:45:41,150
That sounds very professional.

983
00:45:41,150 --> 00:45:44,710
Yes, notice how I didn't say no directly.

984
00:45:44,710 --> 00:45:48,750
That brings us to an important skill, disagreeing politely.

985
00:45:48,750 --> 00:45:52,150
Yes, this is critical in business English.

986
00:45:52,150 --> 00:45:55,490
Instead of saying, I disagree, what can we say?

987
00:45:55,490 --> 00:45:58,750
You can say, I see your point, but...

988
00:45:58,750 --> 00:46:00,350
That's a great one.

989
00:46:00,350 --> 00:46:03,950
Or I understand where you're coming from, however...

990
00:46:03,950 --> 00:46:05,330
Very polite.

991
00:46:05,330 --> 00:46:09,310
Another useful phrase is, that's a valid point, but we may need to consider

992
00:46:09,310 --> 00:46:12,310
These phrases soften the disagreement.

993
00:46:12,310 --> 00:46:14,310
Let's practice this with an example.

994
00:46:14,310 --> 00:46:19,310
Okay, we think the price should be reduced by 20%.

995
00:46:19,310 --> 00:46:21,310
I understand your concern about the cost,

996
00:46:21,310 --> 00:46:24,310
but reducing it by 20% would be difficult for us.

997
00:46:24,310 --> 00:46:27,310
That sounds much better than just saying no.

998
00:46:27,310 --> 00:46:30,310
Now let's talk about asking for clarification.

999
00:46:30,310 --> 00:46:34,310
Yes, sometimes you don't fully understand something.

1000
00:46:34,310 --> 00:46:37,310
You can say, could you clarify what you mean by that?

1001
00:46:37,310 --> 00:46:43,210
by that? Or could you explain that in more detail? Another good one is, just to make

1002
00:46:43,210 --> 00:46:48,910
sure I understand. That's very useful. Asking questions is actually a strong

1003
00:46:48,910 --> 00:46:54,910
negotiation skill. Absolutely. It shows you are engaged and thoughtful. Now let's

1004
00:46:54,910 --> 00:47:00,870
move to making offers. Yes, this is where negotiation becomes more active. You

1005
00:47:00,870 --> 00:47:08,130
can say we can offer or we'd be willing to another powerful phrase is we could

1006
00:47:08,130 --> 00:47:14,910
agree to this if ah that's conditional negotiation let's do a role play great

1007
00:47:14,910 --> 00:47:20,550
we need the delivery within 10 days we could agree to a 10-day delivery if

1008
00:47:20,550 --> 00:47:26,170
the order volume is increased that's a perfect negotiation sentence now let's

1009
00:47:26,170 --> 00:47:28,410
Let's talk about responding to offers.

1010
00:47:28,410 --> 00:47:31,390
Yes, you need to react carefully.

1011
00:47:31,390 --> 00:47:33,990
You can say, that sounds reasonable.

1012
00:47:33,990 --> 00:47:36,290
Or that could work for us.

1013
00:47:36,290 --> 00:47:39,210
Another one is, let me think about that.

1014
00:47:39,210 --> 00:47:40,970
Good for buying time.

1015
00:47:40,970 --> 00:47:42,610
And if you're not happy?

1016
00:47:42,610 --> 00:47:45,890
You can say, I'm not sure that would work for us.

1017
00:47:45,890 --> 00:47:48,890
Or we might need to reconsider that point.

1018
00:47:48,890 --> 00:47:51,310
Now let's talk about compromise.

1019
00:47:51,310 --> 00:47:53,410
This is the heart of negotiation.

1020
00:47:53,410 --> 00:47:56,050
Yes, both sides give something.

1021
00:47:56,050 --> 00:47:59,170
You can say, we're willing to meet you halfway.

1022
00:47:59,170 --> 00:48:01,370
That's a very common phrase.

1023
00:48:01,370 --> 00:48:03,890
Or let's find a middle ground.

1024
00:48:03,890 --> 00:48:05,370
Another great one.

1025
00:48:05,370 --> 00:48:06,750
Example time.

1026
00:48:06,750 --> 00:48:09,490
We want a 15% discount.

1027
00:48:09,490 --> 00:48:13,330
We can't offer 15%, but we're willing to meet you halfway

1028
00:48:13,330 --> 00:48:14,650
at 10%.

1029
00:48:14,650 --> 00:48:16,370
Perfect compromise.

1030
00:48:16,370 --> 00:48:19,050
Now let's talk about handling pressure.

1031
00:48:19,050 --> 00:48:22,530
Yes, sometimes negotiations get intense.

1032
00:48:22,530 --> 00:48:25,810
You can say, we need some time to consider this.

1033
00:48:25,810 --> 00:48:29,490
or let's take a moment to review our options.

1034
00:48:29,490 --> 00:48:32,090
This helps you stay calm and professional.

1035
00:48:32,090 --> 00:48:34,770
Now let's do a longer role play.

1036
00:48:34,770 --> 00:48:35,930
Great idea.

1037
00:48:35,930 --> 00:48:37,890
Thank you for meeting with us today.

1038
00:48:37,890 --> 00:48:40,690
We'd like to discuss the contract terms.

1039
00:48:40,690 --> 00:48:41,530
Thank you.

1040
00:48:41,530 --> 00:48:43,250
We appreciate the opportunity.

1041
00:48:43,250 --> 00:48:45,290
Our main objective is to finalize

1042
00:48:45,290 --> 00:48:47,050
the agreement this week.

1043
00:48:47,050 --> 00:48:47,970
That sounds good.

1044
00:48:47,970 --> 00:48:50,050
However, we may need a bit more time

1045
00:48:50,050 --> 00:48:51,730
for internal approval.

1046
00:48:51,730 --> 00:48:52,810
I understand.

1047
00:48:52,810 --> 00:48:55,930
Would you be open to setting a tentative deadline?

1048
00:48:55,930 --> 00:48:57,650
Yes, that could work.

1049
00:48:57,650 --> 00:49:00,930
We're aiming for a price of $10,000.

1050
00:49:00,930 --> 00:49:03,970
I see your point, but that price is slightly lower

1051
00:49:03,970 --> 00:49:05,610
than our expectations.

1052
00:49:05,610 --> 00:49:07,210
What would you suggest?

1053
00:49:07,210 --> 00:49:09,130
We could agree to $12,000,

1054
00:49:09,130 --> 00:49:11,970
but we'd include additional support services.

1055
00:49:11,970 --> 00:49:13,170
That's interesting.

1056
00:49:13,170 --> 00:49:14,690
Let me think about that.

1057
00:49:14,690 --> 00:49:15,690
Of course.

1058
00:49:15,690 --> 00:49:18,690
We're willing to meet you halfway at $11,000

1059
00:49:18,690 --> 00:49:20,570
if the support is included.

1060
00:49:20,570 --> 00:49:22,210
That sounds reasonable.

1061
00:49:22,210 --> 00:49:24,030
That was a great example.

1062
00:49:24,030 --> 00:49:27,230
Yes, and notice how smooth the conversation was.

1063
00:49:27,230 --> 00:49:30,550
Now, let's talk about closing the negotiation.

1064
00:49:30,550 --> 00:49:32,270
Very important step.

1065
00:49:32,270 --> 00:49:35,570
You can say, so we're agreed on...

1066
00:49:35,570 --> 00:49:38,630
Or, let's summarize what we've decided.

1067
00:49:38,630 --> 00:49:41,990
Another one is, we're happy to move forward with this.

1068
00:49:41,990 --> 00:49:44,190
That shows agreement clearly.

1069
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:46,310
Let's do a closing example.

1070
00:49:46,310 --> 00:49:47,230
Sure.

1071
00:49:47,230 --> 00:49:50,790
So, we're agreed on the price and delivery timeline.

1072
00:49:50,790 --> 00:49:52,430
Yes, that's correct.

1073
00:49:52,430 --> 00:49:55,230
Great, we'll prepare the final contract.

1074
00:49:55,230 --> 00:49:57,030
Looking forward to working together.

1075
00:49:57,030 --> 00:49:59,230
That sounds very professional.

1076
00:49:59,230 --> 00:50:00,430
Exactly.

1077
00:50:00,430 --> 00:50:03,310
Now, let's talk about common mistakes.

1078
00:50:03,310 --> 00:50:05,590
Yes, this is very important.

1079
00:50:05,590 --> 00:50:08,470
Mistake one, being too direct.

1080
00:50:08,470 --> 00:50:11,630
Saying this is too expensive can sound rude.

1081
00:50:11,630 --> 00:50:14,990
Instead, say the price seems a bit high for us.

1082
00:50:14,990 --> 00:50:16,310
Much better.

1083
00:50:16,310 --> 00:50:18,990
Mistake two, not listening.

1084
00:50:18,990 --> 00:50:21,990
Negotiation is a two-way conversation.

1085
00:50:21,990 --> 00:50:25,310
Mistake three, using emotional language.

1086
00:50:25,310 --> 00:50:27,470
Stay calm and professional.

1087
00:50:27,470 --> 00:50:30,310
Mistake four, not being clear.

1088
00:50:30,310 --> 00:50:33,030
Always express your position clearly.

1089
00:50:33,030 --> 00:50:35,030
Let's do a quick practice.

1090
00:50:35,030 --> 00:50:37,270
I'll say something, you improve it.

1091
00:50:37,270 --> 00:50:38,190
I'll start.

1092
00:50:38,190 --> 00:50:39,990
Your offer is bad.

1093
00:50:39,990 --> 00:50:43,150
I'm not sure this offer meets our expectations.

1094
00:50:43,150 --> 00:50:44,430
Much better.

1095
00:50:44,430 --> 00:50:46,510
We can't accept this.

1096
00:50:46,510 --> 00:50:50,150
Unfortunately, we're unable to accept this proposal.

1097
00:50:50,150 --> 00:50:51,190
Perfect.

1098
00:50:51,190 --> 00:50:52,990
Now, let's wrap up.

1099
00:50:52,990 --> 00:50:55,750
We covered so many useful phrases today.

1100
00:50:55,750 --> 00:50:59,270
From starting a negotiation to closing it professionally.

1101
00:50:59,270 --> 00:51:03,310
Remember, the key is to be polite, clear, and confident.

1102
00:51:03,310 --> 00:51:05,990
Practice these phrases again and again.

1103
00:51:05,990 --> 00:51:08,910
Try using them in real meetings or role plays.

1104
00:51:08,910 --> 00:51:11,710
Now it's time for our question of the day.

1105
00:51:11,710 --> 00:51:13,830
Have you ever been in a negotiation?

1106
00:51:13,830 --> 00:51:14,990
What did you say?

1107
00:51:14,990 --> 00:51:18,310
Or, what is one phrase you want to start using?

1108
00:51:18,310 --> 00:51:20,550
Write your answers in the comments below.

1109
00:51:20,550 --> 00:51:22,830
We love reading your responses.

1110
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:25,110
Thank you so much for joining us today.

1111
00:51:25,110 --> 00:51:29,090
Keep practicing, stay confident, and keep improving your English.

1112
00:51:29,090 --> 00:51:30,510
See you in the next episode.

1113
00:51:30,510 --> 00:51:30,950
Goodbye.
